-- title:
--   Pointwise lower bound for the kernel on cone-restricted cubes of side $h$
-- statement:
--   Work in Euclidean space $\mathbb{R}^d$. Let $\Gamma$ be a configuration, let $k : \mathbb{R}^d \times \mathbb{R}^d \to [0,\infty]$ satisfy $\mathrm{KernelBounds}(\Gamma, \alpha, \Lambda, k)$, and let $\alpha > 0$. Let $F$ be a family of reference cones for $\Gamma$ of aperture $\theta$, with $F.\mathrm{cone}\,m$ the cone indexed by $m$ and $F.\mathrm{shrunkAt}\,m\,\rho\,x$ that cone shrunk by $\rho$ and placed at $x$. For a mesh $h$ write $A_h^{V}(u) = \{ s \in A_h(u) : V \subseteq \Gamma(s)\}$ for the cone-restricted cube of side $h$ at $u$, and $\mathbf{1}_A$ for the $[0,\infty]$-valued indicator of $A$.
--
--   Let $h > 0$, let $x, y \in h\mathbb{Z}^d$ be points of the scaled lattice with
--   $$\sqrt{d}\,h < \|x - y\|,$$
--   let $m, n \in \mathbb{R}^d$ be arbitrary indices, and let
--   $$s \in A_h^{F.\mathrm{cone}\,m}(x), \qquad t \in A_h^{F.\mathrm{cone}\,n}(y).$$
--   Then
--   $$\Lambda^{-1}\Big(\mathbf{1}_{F.\mathrm{shrunkAt}\,m\,(h\sqrt{d})\,x}(y) + \mathbf{1}_{F.\mathrm{shrunkAt}\,n\,(h\sqrt{d})\,y}(x)\Big)\,(2\sqrt{d})^{-d-\alpha}\,\|x-y\|^{-d-\alpha} \;\le\; k(s,t).$$
--
--   This is the mesh-$h$ form of the pointwise lower bound, and the point of stating it directly rather than transporting the unit-mesh version is that the constant $(2\sqrt{d})^{-d-\alpha}$ does not depend on $h$: the comparison $\|s-t\| \le 2\sqrt{d}\,\|x-y\|$ between points of two well-separated cubes of side $h$ is scale-invariant. Integrating it over the two cubes yields the lower bound for the averaged discrete kernel at mesh $h$ with the very same constants as at mesh $1$.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** Values are in $\mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}^{\infty}$, with real factors injected by `ENNReal.ofReal`. The indices $m, n$ are unconstrained; the substance of the hypotheses on them is carried entirely by the memberships of $s$ and $t$.
-- source:
